 "title": "The 12 divisors of 72 as an area",
 "caption": "Every divisor of 72 = 2³ × 3² is a power of 2 times a power of 3: the 4 × 3 = 12 cells of this grid. Widths 1, 2, 4, 8 add to 15 and heights 1, 3, 9 add to 13, so the cells add to 15 × 13 = 195.",
 "alt": "A grid of 12 rectangles, widths 1, 2, 4, 8 and heights 1, 3, 9, each labelled with its area, a divisor of 72.",
 "description": [
  "Widths are the powers of 2 up to 2³: 1, 2, 4, 8, which add to 15.",
  "Heights are the powers of 3 up to 3²: 1, 3, 9, which add to 13.",
  "Each cell's area is a divisor of 72, and all 12 divisors appear: d(72) = 4 × 3 = 12.",
  "The cells add up to the whole rectangle: σ(72) = 15 × 13 = 195."
 ],
